Changes in version 0.4.3
 * tsggplot: added support for zoo objects
 * tsggplot: added support for yearly and hourly xts frequencies, verified weekly/daily
 * tsggplot: fixed x-position handling for xts series so plotted data lines up with axis ticks (affected yearly/hourly/monthly/quarterly xts)
 * tsggplot: fixed line_to_middle centering for xts series (frequency() was unreliable, e.g. near-zero for hourly data)
 * tsggplotly: rewritten with working custom hover text and a real secondary y-axis (built from the same axis metadata used to draw the plot); removed dead commented-out code
 * tsggplot: quiet argument now wired through consistently (returns axis metadata alongside the plot when FALSE), matching tsplot's behavior
 * tsggplot: fixed overlapping yearly x-axis labels on longer series / narrower plots
 * tsggplotly: fixed overlapping yearly x-axis labels in the interactive plot too (the static fix above doesn't carry over automatically); new x_tick_mode argument ("thin"/"auto") lets you choose between our own overlap-avoidance or handing tick placement to Plotly
Changes in version 0.4.2
 * Load XLSX files as data.table instead of data.frame
Changes in version 0.4.1
 * Bringing tstools back to CRAN, maintenance release.
Changes in version 0.3.6.1
